Fillets: an analytic blend cut to the end by a face at the end tangent to
the other contact's face, the cut ending past the spine's end vertex on
their edge's line (mitcad#236).

The case: a bar whose edge along the floor is rounded with 3, and beside it
a block that reaches further out, its own edge along the floor rounded with
8, its floor going 0.073 mm further than the bar's. The block's face beside
the bar is a step between the two profiles, which narrows to a point at the
vertex V where the bar's rounding comes tangent to the floor. The step's
foot is rounded with 0.5 (its edge with the floor, 0.073 long, on
tangentially up the block's rounding). Near V the step is lower than the
ball: the contact on it leaves the step across its edge with the bar's
rounding B, and B cuts the blend all along from there to V
(ChFi3d_KPartCutToEnd). That cut ends where the blend's other contact meets
the edge Eq between its face Fo (the floor) and B at V; but Eq ends at V,
and the contact, 0.5 off the step, meets Eq's line only 0.5 past V. No end
was found, the corner (PerformOneCorner, OnSame) cut the walked blend with
B instead and looked for the floor's edge with the block's rounding to
cross B, which passes 0.9 micrometres above it: "the edge beside the end
does not cross the face at the end".

Where Fo and B are tangent along Eq (B rounds Fo off there) and the face N
the contact leaves narrows to a point at V (the spine's end edge and N's
edge E with B leave V the same way, within 0.25 rad), their surfaces go on
meeting along Eq's line beyond V. Not where N narrows to a point at E's
other end too: a sliver of N between B and two faces, which another
blend's contact leaves across E as well (a window's floor rounded on both
edges up to a pillar's rounded end), whose corners cut them as before.
The end Q is now taken there, on Eq's curve continued beyond V and on both
surfaces within the tolerance: a new vertex at Q ends the blend (a
singular end, as at Q on Eq), B grows up to the cut, Eq is prolonged
beyond V to Q (ChFi3d_ProlongEdgeBeyondVertex), and the spine's end edge,
under the blend, is cut at V with no side kept.
The piece P whose contact leaves its face may lie on the end edge itself
(the step's foot on a rounding that a smaller rounding of the bar meets
tangentially): it then still has the parameters of that edge's whole blend,
extended past the edge, at its end, which the corner sets at an OnSame end.
There its end section is taken through its other contact's point (by
bisection on the edge, as Q's), and its parameters at that end are those of
its points (on a closed contact line, in the period that keeps the piece's
direction from its other end); restored when no pieces are added. The same
end where a plate's top meets a cylindrical wall, rounded concave up to the
plate's corner rounding tangent to the wall, builds as the file's (the
rounding there was built before too, by the corner).

On the stored design the step's foot builds as in the file: every face of
the result lies on the file's (the boolean differences with the file's
body are empty both ways), the change of volume 0.04 % off the file's, and
the bar's rounding grown past the step by the file's 0.41 mm2. Tests:
geometry/tests/test_fillet_corners.cpp, the step beside the rounded bar
(failing without the patch) and beside a notch rounded tangent to the
block's rounding, both against the block alone rounded less what lies in
the bar's profile, and a tab's top rounded concave up to its side
roundings tangent to a curved wall, against the material under the
rounding's torus within the tab's outline.
